From: AdobeWine
Subject: [PATCH] msi: Do not delete files on rollback that this install did not create.

Wine rolls InstallFiles back by running RemoveFiles with every component back at its previous state, so it deleted
every file of a component that was not installed before, whether this install had written it or not, and including
files that were on disk before it (overwritten without a backup). Acrobat 26.002's patch carries the VC++ 14.44
merge modules for system32 and syswow64; when its PatchFiles failed (mspatcha), the rollback deleted the prefix's
vcruntime140, concrt140, msvcp140_1, msvcp140_atomic_wait, msvcp140_codecvt_ids and vccorlib140, and every Adobe app
stopped starting. Windows restores overwritten files from its rollback backup and leaves alone what it did not
install. On rollback a file is now removed only if this install created it.
Test: Acrobat 26.002 MSI with its patch on a clean prefix copy: fails at PatchFiles as before; afterwards system32
and syswow64 hold the same VC++ files as before the install (was: six deleted from each), and Acrobat's own files
are removed as before (3 files left in Acrobat DC, as without the patch).
---
diff --git a/dlls/msi/files.c b/dlls/msi/files.c
index e7686d0..aedb893 100644
--- a/dlls/msi/files.c
+++ b/dlls/msi/files.c
@@ -407,6 +407,8 @@ static void schedule_install_files(MSIPACKAGE *package)
         MSICOMPONENT *comp = file->Component;
 
         file->state = calculate_install_state( package, file );
+        file->existed = file->state != msifs_missing && file->state != msifs_skipped &&
+                        msi_get_file_attributes( package, file->TargetPath ) != INVALID_FILE_ATTRIBUTES;
         if (file->state == msifs_overwrite && (comp->Attributes & msidbComponentAttributesNeverOverwrite))
         {
             TRACE("not overwriting %s\n", debugstr_w(file->TargetPath));
@@ -1570,6 +1572,14 @@ UINT ACTION_RemoveFiles( MSIPACKAGE *package )
         if (comp->Action != INSTALLSTATE_ABSENT || comp->Installed == INSTALLSTATE_SOURCE)
             continue;
 
+        /* Rolling back undoes only what this install did. Windows restores overwritten files from its backup;
+         * without one, leave a file that was already there (a shared runtime in system32) instead of deleting it. */
+        if (package->need_rollback && (file->state != msifs_installed || file->existed))
+        {
+            TRACE("rollback: keeping %s, not created by this install\n", debugstr_w(file->TargetPath));
+            continue;
+        }
+
         if (comp->assembly && !comp->assembly->application)
             continue;
 
diff --git a/dlls/msi/msipriv.h b/dlls/msi/msipriv.h
index 0efc367..99ad03b 100644
--- a/dlls/msi/msipriv.h
+++ b/dlls/msi/msipriv.h
@@ -620,6 +620,7 @@ typedef struct tagMSIFILE
     INT Attributes;
     INT Sequence;
     msi_file_state state;
+    BOOL existed; /* the target was on disk before InstallFiles */
     LPWSTR  TargetPath;
     BOOL IsCompressed;
     MSIFILEHASHINFO hash;
